listen andy is uh here with us now lisa  good morning thank you very much indeed  for joining us on the programme this  morning and we'll talk about your new  job in just a second um could christmas  be ruined i really hope not i mean like  every family around the country i  desperately hope not but i think largely  this is now in the government's gift the  vast majority of people as far as i can  see are doing what is being asked of  them wearing masks getting the booster  jab social distancing  you know my my little boy school has got  its doors and windows open trying to you  know increase ventilation even in the  cold people are people are trying their  best but there are some big holes in the  government's plans particularly around  travel  and the experience of coming back  somebody who's just served a shadow  foreign secretary i know this well and  taking a day to pcr test is very  shambolic for a lot of people the  government isn't even checking up on the  majority of those tests and whether  people are getting them or not and many  of the companies that are supposed to  provide them they don't even turn up  people don't get the results there are  there are big problems here and we need  the government to step up and do their  parts because we're doing ours  we've heard from nicolas sturgeon she  wants us to self-isolate for eight days  and then take a pcr test if we've  traveled overseas i think the bigger  issue actually is something that yvette  cooper who is our newly appointed shadow  home secretary has been saying as chair  of the home affairs select committee for  some time why aren't we taking asking  people to take pre-departure tests at  the moment people are getting onto  planes they're flying back into britain  from many countries with very high rates  of covid where there may be an omicron  variant they're then getting off the  plane and traveling home on public  transport where they're then asked to  take a pcr test and self-isolate that  does leave a great big hole in our  defenses and we've raised this  repeatedly with the government for 18  months and yet nothing has been done we  can't keep making the same mistakes over  and over again this is how we get the  situation where yet again we're debating  whether christmas is going to be ruined  or not  the omicron variant there might not be  any cause for concern so i spoke to  jenny harris the deputy chief medical  officer on saturday evening  and i think it's fair to say that we  just don't quite know enough about it  yet the you know how much the booster  jab the jab actually works in relation  to omicron you know how how  transmissible it is these are all things  that the scientists are working around  the clock to try and work out what we do  know right now though is that the  biggest variant in the uk the most  prevalent variant is the delta variant  the one that we've we've been dealing  with already we know that the vaccine is  effective against the delta variant so i  think the message from all of us across  the political spectrum putting aside our  differences  is please go and get the vaccine please  go and get your boosted job because that  will make a big difference to the  national effort three more cases i'm  just being told have been found in  scotland um not sure about you know  what happened for them to  be  covered positive but it isn't  necessarily a south africa vaccine  south africa covid variant is it that's  one of the challenges i think that's we  don't know where it's come from i think  that's right and actually what we do  know is that countries that are better  at detecting these things that have  better genomic sequencing in in country  are the ones that are most likely to  find it so it may be possible just as  with the so-called kent variant it's  it's likely that that didn't emerge in  kent it was traced in the uk because  we've got some of the best scientists in  the world and scientific facilities so  it is a problem because by the time you  discover these things you don't know how  far they've traveled but i've been  amazed actually having met with the  scientists that are working on this all  over the world but particularly here in  the uk how sophisticated they are about  tracking these things the first two  cases that were found they were able to  track very very quickly  how they'd come into the uk how those  cases were connected i'm sure they'll be  working on this now and i think there's  no reason for people to panic just do  the right thing follow the guidelines  try and be sensible and let's get  through this like we have done for the  last 18 months let's get through this  together one of the things the  government is doing and i'm sure you'll  applaud them for it is three and a half  million boosters or vaccinations or and  boosters a week is what they're aiming  for and they're hoping to mobilize an  army of volunteers and nhs staff  where does that then leave us with your  old hat on for giving vaccines to other  countries well we've got enough vaccines  to to make sure that the adult  population around the world is  vaccinated why don't we give it to you  well when i came here six months ago  that was the challenge it was the  challenge was to ramp up manufacturing  so that we weren't choosing between  vaccinating people in wigan and  vaccinating people in wuhan that's not  the challenge anymore the challenges the  first time you said that is it no  but the challenge is to get i get wigan  into everything yeah okay yeah i  appreciate it  but we you know the challenge is to get  them out to people across the world and  one of the problems they've had in south  africa and particularly many of the  surrounding countries  is that the healthcare infrastructure  needs to be there the vaccinations have  to arrive quickly enough many of them  arrive just as they're about to expire  so they simply don't have time to get  them into people's arms that's why we've  been critical 