 bring good  jobs and start to bring the spending  power back so that young people don't  have to get out to get on and we can  rebuild our high streets and our  communities that's the agenda that will  be the battleground for not just the  next election but for the future of this  country and i am determined that we are  going to deliver on it yeah so kyocerma  has you know been slowly but surely  getting rid of the left in his um shadow  cabinet where does angela reina fit in  this night well i mean i you know i  didn't even tell her that it was  happening i would say to you first of  all i am the left i mean you know we're  all the left we the labour are  progressives and you know we have  differences  sure but i mean look look we have  differences of opinion  too often that's seen as a problem i  don't think it is and in the last 18  months i've seen angela rayner who's our  deputy leader who is an incredibly  strong woman with her own opinions  showing real authority and leadership in  her role and i've seen a leader in  kiestama who's completely comfortable  with that i can tell you from personal  experience he is not worried about being  around strong northern women who have  their own opinions and that's not having  a choice as far as she's concerned  because she he doesn't decide whether  she's in that role or not one wonders  why he didn't let her know what was  going on well she was elected with her  own mandate that's certainly true but i  think there's been a huge effort on both  of their parts to work together  and to embrace the differences that they  have you can see that they come from  very different backgrounds very  different traditions very different  parts of the country my view is that's  good for labour and you know as far as  reshuffles are concerned i've been  through a lot in the last 11 years most  of them didn't end as well for me as  this one and i've never seen a leader  who has um held back from doing what he  has so far always been he because it's  been common  as far as as far as i know i haven't  spoken to angela but as far as i  understand it he did let her know i  don't know to the extent not to the  extent that you know he was going to do  what he was being sacked but at the end  of the day kay kier  he's our candidate for prime minister  and the gaffer picks the team that's  right that's how it ought to be and i'm  just really pleased that he's  allowed me to get out into the country  so that i can start to stand up for the  people that haven't had a voice in this  system for far too long uh in the  absence of the shadow foreign secretary  who is david lammy now i think talk to  me about what's happening with  afghanistan because it breaks my heart  when i think about some of those people  that we left behind well i suspect that  you'll hear something from david lammy  on afghanistan today because it's an  absolute passion for him when you look  at those boats coming across the channel  one of the boats the boat that sank  recently there was an afghan soldier on  that boat who had said he'd simply given  up hope of a safe legal route opening up  and britain making good on its promise  to protect and support people like him  we will not stop fighting for the people  of afghanistan who helped us over two  decades our soldiers flew into danger in  order to support those people they they  stood with them for two decades so we're  not just making good on our promise to  the afghan people we're making good on  the promise to our armed forces who  fought for the future of afghanistan for  20 years i'm now responsible for afghan  resettlement and i can tell you that  i'll be working with labour councils and  labour mayors around this country to  make sure that we give a warm welcome to  those people when they reach the uk and  david will continue to fight the fight  to make sure that we make good on our  obligations if global britain is to mean  anything it means we stand with the  people who supported us over two decades  listen andy it's always good to talk to  you thank you very much for joining us  thank you

